{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563296-musings-about-an-actual-chronicle","id":1563296,"title":"Musings About an Actual Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-20T22:34:33-07:00","id":1563296,"title":"Musings About an Actual Chronicle","content":"My wife is running for us a Chronicle of V5, my first long experience with the edition. I won't say this will be an Actual Play because I'm not sure what I'll make of this thread, but whatever I put here, you're all welcome to comment, use, criticize, all in all do whatever pleases ya.<br /> <br /> Our story is taking place in the US East Coast, a version with a strong coat of the New England found in the writings of H. P. Lovecraft. Anyone familiar with the place, be aware that for us it is an exotic, distant location we only hear about and wonder about the culture of the natives, so please be patient with any errors.<br /> <br /> Carcosa, a fictional metropolis of a few million inhabitants, has never been a normal place. No few visitants joke (or talk very seriously) of the city's inverted Masquerade: the world must not know what this place is like. In the impossibly clear sky the full moon is always visible, in the nearby lake the water reflects a second, alien sun, people hear stars sing and feel the dark places of the earth caress them with tendrils of shadows. Most Carcosans never saw normalcy in their lives.<br /> <br /> But it is facing an unprecedented disaster. An accident with a cargo ship 2 years ago turned the sea into a horribly toxic hazard. Fortunately the last decades of economic diversification prevented a deeper social crisis, but cleaning is nowhere near completion if possible at all, and there's risk that something escape to the world at large with this contamination, bringing some unwanted outside intervention.<br /> <br /> The mortals share theories about what spilled from the cargo. Oil is a common assumption, but all kinds of compounds are guessed, as the authorities seem evasive on what's it and the known evidence is inconclusive. The creatures that hide in the darkness know better. A thing died there, that shouldn't have been alive for so much time as it did. An undead thousands of years old and riddled with eons of accumulated experiments, blood magic and corruption.<br /> <br /> Now the tainted waters mutate its residents. At first the vampire regency of the city worried if it would affect blood quality and resonance, and moved to stop fishing altogether. Today those fears seem quaint in face of the things that are found with increasing frequency. A few days ago the things started to appear inland, and the PCs were called as a desperate task force to investigate anyone and anything trying to profit from making things worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T22:34:55-07:00","id":1563522,"title":"","content":"The PCs<br /> <br /> We were all Embraced in 1996, though we did not share this information with each other yet in game. That's 30 years before the start of the chronicle, Neonates with some experience. All vampires are of 11th Generation, although one was originally 12th.<br /> <br /> Pretel Sullivan is a mortal. He's a diplomat of sorts, accepted by local factions as liaison between different creatures. This role has been filled by mortals for several generations and he's the current one, receiving several benefits in exchange and a mansion whose total extent and mystical resources are a mystery.<br /> <br /> It has been a huge source of pressure, though, driving Sullivan to all sorts of coping habits, but mainly drugs and lack of self preservation. The constant exposure, some innate trait of his and access to supernatural means to restore health made Sullivan able to function while under the combined effects of all recreational substance known to modern society. The price is just to look like something between a zombie and a walking inflammation, and recently to suffer of memory loss although it may be psychological.<br /> <br /> For the time being Sullivan is off-limits to any vampire as either Ghoul or food. It's uncertain if that's for his services or for his blood being a biological hazard. Either way, he's the youngest PC, being in his mid 30s.<br /> <br /> Sam is a Brazilian small child that came to the US some time after the embrace. He's a boy, but pretends to be a girl with a Gothic-Lolita style, the other PCs don't know yet that he's actually a boy. He's a vlogger and influencer with some local fame.<br /> <br /> Having been Embraced by a show runner that were secretly both a vampire and the head of a child trafficking and prostitution ring, today Sam tries to find dirt on every adult that works with children's shows, assuming they're part of a major global conspiracy of child trafficking that is the power behind institutions like the Camarilla. Sam is 40 years old in total.<br /> <br /> Drew Blood was Embraced into the Brujah with 28, being now 58. He was then a circumstantial victim that got Embraced out of morality crisis, an old story, and isn't really engaged in politics or almost anything, anyway. The closest he has of usual Brujah rebellion is that he still holds a grudge against his last employer after decades and keeps tabs on children and grandchildren of the old bastard.<br /> <br /> Our group currently meets at the Morrigan's Den, Blood's vintage arcade that still somehow survives with a semblance of profit, partially thanks to patronage of other Brujah, the city's Sheriff and resident tall tale teller, Camael. The Den also sells occult stuff, a compromise after years of new age customers asking if it was an occult store because of the name and possibly another explanation for it making enough to stay afloat. On an unrelated note, besides the owner the night shift is run by a legit Get of Fenris Cliath. We found out she is a werewolf infiltrated recently, but Drew doesn't care and just gave her a promotion to cover her security service to the store.<br /> <br /> At 60 years old, Victor Shadowthorn is from the Lasombra and, still unknown to the group and the city at large, a Diablerist, originally from the 12th Generation and the only in the group now at Blood Potency 2. He's a businessman and a game developer struggling every night to code something under his Bane.<br /> <br /> Victor got the attention of his sire after building a successful company out of just a single indie game still back in the early 90s. VoidByte Soft is now a powerhouse and Shadowthorn is the main shareholder and CEO. His single crime to local vampiric law was against a Ventrue who dared try to destroy the company, and his end is thought to be work of the Second Inquisition (which, to be fair, it would be anyway).<br /> <br /> Given Carcosa being now it is, Obtenebration's powers have a skewed psychological effect on natives, mortal or vampires. Fear/discomfort effects from exposure to its shadows are done in reverse to them, they find it soothing, warm, cuddly and nostalgic, as the city has a natural Obtenebration-like effect that everyone is used to feeling from time to time (children encounter it on a weekly basis). Since Shadowthorn is a local he's used to this and uses his signature power to put people at ease. Since his sire is not a local, he finds this reaction creepy as hell and rarely uses Obtenebration directly on people.<br /> <br /> My own character is 62 years old, despite the appearance of 20. Hoshino Y\u016bbi arrived just a few days ago fleeing Japan. Like Shadowthorn she's a very successful game dev since the 80s as part of the D\u014djin scene in T\u014dky\u014d. Contrary to Shadowthorn, being a woman with low social skills and too many opinions made her a victim rather than star. The most profitable franchise in Japanese videogame history was mostly her doing, but before the final release her name got erased from records and her murder arranged.<br /> <br /> But someone among the traitors went above and beyond and got the sweetest deal of their dreams. The hired assassin asked a heft price for an over the top service. First her body was extensively modified to make her a pretty doll, then she was killed, turned undead and sold to them back as a slave, all the tricks needed to keep her under control given to them. Y\u016bbi has no idea yet what kind of dealing went on, only now she's slowly comprehending how bizarrely out of place was such a deal, and she has few memories of her absent Tzimisce sire. Neither does she know much about her clan outside a few recent pointers.<br /> <br /> Japan went through a commotion less than a week ago in the game, as a terrorist attack left Yasukuni Shrine in ruins. What Y\u016bbi can say of the event is that she noticed the guards of her prison/office leaving, and a woman came and took her out of it, a woman she found out to be a Kitsune (general sense, not necessarily the Fera splat). She found herself less than an hour later in a private jet, flying to the US in the august company of the younger brother of the Emperor. She is understandably more curious about her release than her Embrace. She was brought to Carcosa and given a pretty decent Haven, an old but safe Cold War bunker still in working conditions.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Margarida is from Acapulco, Mexico. At 86 years old <i>at the time of Embrace,</i> she's seen as an Elder by some, especially in conversation when she's not around. She has a successful business franchise in the city selling plants and flowers, goes to the church twice a week, work with Y\u016bbi as volunteer at a Soup Kitchen, goes around town sharing gossip like a pro, attend to club reunions where she teaches shibari and dishes nightly brutal punishment to those who mistreat animals.<br /> <br /> No one knows why her sire, born when she was 30, chose her for the Embrace. Most accepted is the theory that her fierce protection of wild and domesticated life alike was a main factor, but many find her ties to the BDSM community at least suggestive, and the most actually told thesis is that she prove her right to Gangrel resilience by outliving her great grandnephew, Rameses III.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T16:00:42-07:00","id":1563548,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">VTM meets Lovecraft? Sounds Awesome!<br /> <br /> The setting reminds me a bit of Shadow Over Innsmouth.<br /> <br /> The biological hazard subplot sounds very cool as well. Especially if it mutates, vampires that partake too much. If you need some inspiration, Night Horror Blood Spilled in VTR 2 has some pretty cool ideas for kindred diseases and infections. Very effective at creating dread for vampire PCs, who normally are normally only afraid of their typical weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Some other comments :</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s a Kindred named Drew <i>Blood. </i>That\u2019s funny.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Lasombra game Dev is definitely one of the ideas of all time. (I like it.) Maybe he can lean into leading a game team. Poor team. Crunch time is going to be rough with a Lasombra.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Love the reversed Obtenebration effect. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character seems involved in some pretty heavy stuff, pretty cool. (I assume you\u2019re aware of controversies surrounding Yasukuni Shrine. Is that why you destroyed it in your background? Feel free to ignore. I don\u2019t want to hijack your thread with political controversies.)</span></span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some follow-up questions :</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is Sam a Malkavian? It wasn\u2019t mentioned, but assumed the conspiracy theory\u2019s focus was the malkavian part.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is one player playing a mortal?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do you plan on using the mythos at all?</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T17:45:25-07:00","id":1563549,"title":"","content":"All questions are welcome, including politics.<br /> <br /> Part of the ST's inspiration was a game called Dredge that's heavily based on Innsmouth, but the most direct influence was The King in Yellow, which is precursor and major influence to the Mythos.<br /> <br /> I don't know if she'll use the Mythos proper, but it's definitely on the table. <hr /><br /> For now the plot revolves around sea life. As far as we know, the contamination didn't reach humans or mammals yet, so no vampires are at risk. Well, maybe from Sullivan, if he ever get bitten we'll find out if a vampire can overdose.<br /> <br /> But oh boy, what sea life. The least mutated creatures are Snapping Turtles that grew to the size of a two-seat sofa. Which is terrible news being Snapping Turtles, those things can take out a finger when they're the size of a small dog.<br /> <br /> Three days ago we heard of a weird shark with glowing mouth that was spitting a bizarre goo over the beach. Our Lasombra also rescued an employee of his that had been locked in the bathroom for three days to hide from a giant eel that managed to wander on land like a snake. The next morning some people across thr city were reporting glowing electric fish in pools and bathrooms, at night we found out a thing resembling a Castlevania Merman getting into the water treatment plant and throwing the mutant fish into the clean water, it was sabotage by what seems to be a Deep One.<br /> <br /> And things are only getting worse. Now we're in a full crisis. Some of the sea mutants are forming an ecosystem in land. Many of the mutant fish are intelligent and understand English. We're trying to control at least two colonies of giant anthropophagous crabs with human mouths that laugh like Kefka and have the powers of the Blood Brothers. There's also at least two psychic flying crabs around that at least don't eat mammals and, since they're telepaths, can be communicated with, so we're trying to use them for intel.<br /> <br /> I helped the local Garou pack with the autopsy of one of the spitting sharks (they multiplied a little) and the fucking thing shouldn't be possible, it's body is composed of soft heavy metals, chlorine based organic compounds and absolutely no water. It also has almost no recognizable organs. One of the Garou is also the District Attorney and we tipped him on a nightclub that was capturing more mutant fish to use as attractions in the dance floor. And we are now investigating a plot to smuggle mutant seafood out of town to reignite fishing in the city regardless of everything wrong with the fish and the risk of this nightmare spreading to the rest of the country, maybe the world. <hr /><br /> Tell me about working with a Lasombra coder. We found out one of the seafood conspirators is a gambling addict and we're building a Pachinko parlor to capture data and hack his things, so now I'm working in the game itself with him and Sam (who's good with networks and front end). Fron time to time he has to accept some shit to Win at a Cost and be able to do any work. <hr /><br /> I can't say I didn't appreciated Yasukuni being blown up in the game, but it was actually the ST's doing. My wife hates the place with a vengeance and made a whole plot about the attack. My escape from Japan is entirely her doing.<br /> <br /> But yeah, my char was basically a work and sex slave for 30 years, still working in the franchise she started to be spared the worse: frenzy with a victim of their choosing. She was promised in no uncertain terms at the time that if she did not cooperate her next meal would be her parents.<br /> <br /> At least that did gave her access to a computer with internet. Heavily watched, but she could follow the news about the outside world and stuff, which was necessary to keep her skills useful. <hr /><br /> Yes and yes. I forgot to mention, but Sam is a Malkavian. And one of the players wanted to do a mortal. He usually prefers to play as mortal in WoD unless it's Changeling. <hr /><br /> We have the mortal, child Malk, disinterested Brujah, Lasombra techbro, Tzimisce artistic game dev and Gangrel octogenarian. Half are immigrants, which is relevant because ICE is with the Second Inquisition. Also some of the people from our Backgrounds, etc were chosen by the ST to also be some mystery on their own.<br /> <br /> Also may be relevant: most of us have been house ruled in some way. I've got the original Tzimisce spread with Auspex rather than Dominate, Sullivan was built as Deadly Mortal, which means a very powerful starting sheet, Sam has several extra XP points in exchange of a homebrew Child Flaw and Shadowthorn is built with one extra Blood Potency, -1 Humanity and an extra 2 dots Flaw for the Diablerie, with the Flaw being custom made to screw him over royally, basically a version of Haunted that does include the Wraith itself being around for real.<br /> <br /> Currently I'm the expert Auspex user with a dash of Animalism that gave me as Famulus a crazy pigeon that thinks he's a German duke cursed by a witch. My character also doesn't have the internal concept of needing a car or to be able to fend for herself, she came from a society where public transportation work and gun violence is rare enough for high profile politicians to use it. Being <i>allowed</i> to drive or to fight is fine. Being <u><i><b>required</b></i></u> to is simply alien or, better yet, prehistoric to her. And for now she won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T10:57:23-07:00","id":1563574,"title":"","content":"Some of the regular NPCs.<br /> <br /> The city has two Regents, being Anarch territory despite copying many Camarilla terminology. The Regents are broodmates, childer of the same Toreador sire.<br /> <br /> Despite that neither consider themselves much of a Toreador. Rafael dedicated his existence to only one art form: that of beating the crap out of others. He also likes cooking and Elvis.<br /> <br /> He is rarely seen in the streets, although his most loyal and beloved Ghoul is well known: a lion also known as Elvis whom he spoiled through the ages so thoroughly the beast can't live without a personal cook anymore.<br /> <br /> Elise does appreciate all forms of art, and she's a skilled gardener. Her most fearsome defense is a field of ancient Blood Roses mutated by her Vitae.<br /> <br /> But even before the Embrace she was already both loyal and Blood Bound to her grandfather, so today Elise Giovanni stands both as Regent and local head of the Hecata, being a master Necromancer.<br /> <br /> Camael is an enforcer of vampire law, but he's also a consummate lier. He claims to be from Carthage, which would be around 22 centuries ago or longer. He also claims to have invented the telemarketing, control time, that his sword was forged by the king of demons, he was the secret behind Mithras's success in London, the Beatles were his work and he got the greatest record on all machines at Morrigan's Den, but there was a blackout that wiped it and now we're have to believe his word.<br /> <br /> Also he is 5th or 4th Generation depending on the night, but his victims always survive the Kiss because they're superior to common mortals, as he only feeds from people who practice yoga and crossfit and eat organic food. In his favor, it was confirmed that he can tell a mortal's diet and blood test by smell, and refuse to approach those who drink too much soda or have eaten processed food in the last week.<br /> <br /> Jason is the District Attorney and leader of a werewolf pack based in the local university. He has been more focused on the problem with the sea, and so accepts for now any help with it. He's also British, and it seems that most of this pack are not from the US, except the Native woman.<br /> <br /> We also got wind that he's married to the headmistress of the university, a chemist with a passionate specialty in explosives and demolition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T10:58:53-07:00","id":1563575,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ah, nice! I haven\u2019t played Dredge, but any game with \u2018\u2019fishermen meets sea horrors\u2019\u2019 is going to have some lovecraftian inspiration at one point or another, or be compared to one.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t read the King of Yellow but I have second-hand knowledge of the plot. I recognized the city\u2019s name inspiration as well.<br /> <br /> I remember I stated some Mythos Monster for a Call of Cthulhu came I ran using V5 as a base frame. Instead of hunger dice, we had stress dice, which worked in a similar fashion; spells were merit. Worked pretty well</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The plot sounds positively insane; I love it.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of something that I hear or read that horror is often goofy at heart.<br /> <br /> Is the game tone more serious or are your characters also aware of the insanity of the situation?<br /> <br /> The metal sharks also suspiciously remind me of Gyo! Is your wife a Junji Ito reader per chance? </span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yeah, that\u2019s rough for the Lasombra coder, lol.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it sounds like an idea i would also love playing if i ever play masquerade again. I\u2019m a sucker for Kindred with curses that actually make their lives harder. This is why I love VTR Nosferatu, who craves social interactions with humans.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yeah, Yasukuni Shrine is .... problematic, to say the least. Somewhat good news: I read a few weeks ago that they banned military cosplay on its grounds.<br /> <br /> As for your character, cool concept, but damn, that\u2019s a heavy past! <br /> <br /> I tend to shy away from sexual violence for my characters. I can suffer from character bleeds, which does help in acting but it\u2019s heavy when those kinds of subjects are involved. I remember once, I literally cried and felt trapped when one of my characters got sequestrated in a Savage World Pathfinder game. I had to take a step back and remind myself that it <i>is </i>a game afterall.<br /> <br /> I hope she\u2019s in a better spot in that hellish oilscape.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Honestly, it\u2019s a cool Malkavian concept. His conspiracy focus is entirely justified from his living experience. Pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Kinda ironic that it\u2019s not a fishmalk in a game with so many weird fish!</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ICE as the second inquisition works pretty well to establish them as unlikable, cool idea. I personally used the Cheiron Group with an SCP-foundation vibe for my game to make them as unambiguously evil as I could. Sometimes you do need a bad guy.<br /> <br /> Does Sullivan\u2019s player fin dit harder to find relevance given the lack of discipline? Do you find that V5 helps in levelling the playing field between kindred characters and mortal characters?<br /> <br /> Trading Auspex for Dominate is a trade I\u2019d make anytime. I\u2019m not a fan of dominate, past cloud memory, to be honest. Do you make Vissicitude an Auspex + Protean Amalgam?<br /> <br /> The diablerie flaw is pretty cool. <br /> <br /> Man, I sympathize with your character\u2019s alien feeling of needing a car. When I came back to Qu\u00e9bec after visiting Japan, I felt like we were so backward in that aspect. I could google any city in Japan and i would get an itinerary using only public transport. Our reality is different for sure, but man, we really need to invest more in public transportation outside of Montr\u00e9al City. I own a car, but I always hated them. I use my E-Bike as much as I can. Pretty much impossible during winter, though.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T23:02:20-07:00","id":1563587,"title":"","content":"Dredge is pretty lovecraftian, albeit not based on the actual Mythos. The area's ocean is being occupied by otherworldly abominations due to an insane researcher trying to contact a &quot;superior&quot; dimension in search of a soul to resurrect, IIRC. Your character is a fisherman and also a researcher trying to figure out what is happening and put an end to it, but there's no combat mechanic, the monsters simply aren't something you can fight. You can only witness the horror and take notes, besides fishing clues and mutant/alien extradimensional fish. <hr /><br /> For the bizarre aspects of the city, I helped her using what's said about Carcosa in the original The King in Yellow book. So, in a sense, it's one particularly faithful use of the inspiration, up to and including some suspicion that maybe this city isn't really solely on the US, but rather in a superimposed plot from a distant planet. <hr /><br /> I think she does read Ito, and even if not she's aware of him and consumes a lot of horror that is based on him and on Lovecraft. She really came to like Cosmic Horror.<br /> <br /> The characters are aware of the insanity, to some degree, especially the foreigners as they know for a fact that this place shouldn't exist even in a world with vampires and stuff.<br /> <br /> But it is serious in the sense that a goofy plot is still pretty real for those within it, so the whole situation is a huge and scary problem, insanity only males it worse as trying to find solutions gets pretty hard when you can't make educated guesses because reality don't want to make sense. <hr />My problem with the Lasombra coder is that the roll is excessively punishing, I do think they got the worse Bane design in the edition.<br /> <br /> Nothing is situational about it, you simply have to roll for it for every single interaction, which puts a chunck of basic game mechanics in the affected zone. On top of that, the Difficulty is 2 + Bane Severity, which means a BP 1 Neonate starts needing a whopping 4 successes when rolling for the right to use a phone or computer. <hr />I have some character bleed, but manageable, and that's mostly in the past. She's definitely in a better place despite everything going on, and for now her bigger worry is the safety of others, especially children.<br /> <br /> Her Haven is close to a school, and one of the places we found anthropophagous crabs was the woods nearby. We're in summer recess, but she wants to take care of this before school year resumes. <hr />Yasukuni is all kinds of problematic, although the real problem isn't the shrine itself, it's what was made with WWII in Japan. By the way, that is a situation the US and Europe have a lot to do with.<br /> <br /> The only reason for what was done at Yasukuni is that instead of doing the thorough education program enacted in Italy and Germany, the &quot;big democracies&quot; decided that helping Japanese fascism to return and stay in power was needed to form a buffer against the Soviets, as genocide is apparently a minor threat compared to the idea of denying rich people their sacred right to control monopolies without state intervention. <hr />Sullivan's player seems fine with things for now and he's used to playing a mortal in a splat game.<br /> <br /> But no, V5 doesn't do a particularly good job at it, the group relying more in skills than powers has a greater effect. Both Legacy and CoD give way more tools to make mortals work in such a game. He's thinking about buying some stuff from Hunter just to compensate, but even that is weak compared to Hunters Hunted alone and its Numina.<br /> <br /> And yes, we're assuming Vicissitude as Auspex based rather than Dominate. <hr />Brazil isn't Japan, but we have a better public transportation situation than the US, I don't know Canada. But still a lot of people buy in the narrative of personal cars being necessary.<br /> <br /> They're not, and shouldn't be. I find bizarre how the program to build the urban structure and cultural narrative for the automobile industry is well known and documented, and still left to its heinous work when everything is already going to hell because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T09:50:30-07:00","id":1563700,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cosmic horror is pretty fun. I\u2019m not very good at picturing what I read so I tend to consume most stories by manga or comics. I do like Junji Ito\u2019s stories a lot, especially those that lean more into cosmic horror rather than body horror; like Hellstar Remina, Black Paradox or Uzumaki. There are also some very nice Lovecraft manga adaptations by Gou Tanabe, very well made and accurate.</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's true that the bane is quite severe. It\u2019s especially hard to deal with in a modern setting. I think it\u2019s more interesting than the mirror bane, but it could be toned down. I\u2019ll admit it\u2019s been a while since I\u2019ve played V5 so I don\u2019t have any solutions at the moment.</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t dislike having characters bleed. I know it\u2019s sometimes seen as a bad thing, but it\u2019s an immersive tool and can be cathartic. It is very much a double-edged blade, however.<br /> <br /> Glad to hear that your character is having it better, though!<br /> <br /> Reminds me of how my own, my Nosferatu Yuka, handles her sire abandonment issues by taking care of other sire-less fledglings.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t doubt for a second that the US and Europe are involved in making it worse.<br /> <br /> Liberals in power will always side with fascism before letting any left-wing government raise power.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hmm\u2026 Yeah, CoD has some extra tools to make powerful mortals; however, seeing how they are nearly defenceless against most supernatural abilities as a result of lacking a supernatural tolerance trait, I thought it would have been a bit better in V5 in which pools are a bit lower by virtue of only adding Discipline + Attribute, instead of Discipline + Attributre + skill.<br /> <br /> Lacking access to cool merits probably makes it harder to create interesting characters.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From my experience in Canada, I haven\u2019t been everywhere (it is a massive country). It\u2019s probably a bit like the US : It varies from city to city.<br /> Montr\u00e9al has a very efficient metro &amp; bus system.<br /> <br /> In my hometown we have a bus system, but it takes anywhere from 30 minutes to 2 hours to reach what would take 5 to 15 minutes in car. It\u2019s inefficient, and people cannot really rely on it to go to work or school without a massive time sink. You\u2019re also pretty much locked in the city. Some buses travel between cities, but it\u2019s travel buses; expansive and only a few buses per day.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T15:22:21-07:00","id":1563711,"title":"","content":"For horror I like books more than comics/manga, but that is mostly because I like the pacing of good horror text, for me it clicks well. For other genres depends. <hr />The original mirror bane was too much of a binary: it's irrelevant or outright incapacitating depending on how much the ST puts reflective surfaces everywhere. It's classic, but bad game design.<br /> <br /> I think the technology thing was a valid attempt but not really a successful one, although the big problem in V5 is the Difficulty being too high. Maybe a cost rather than a roll would be a better compromise. <hr />Character bleed is cathartic indeed. I think the important thing is to be mindful of it and try not to treat it as inherently positive or negative. It's good when it generates interesting experiences and bad when it puts you in a bad place, and all players must just be ready to respect the limits. <hr />CoD has a bigger dice pool difference, but it also gives a lot of Merits and Equipment bonus a mortal can use to do stuff. They're weak, but still very capable. V5 has almost nothing for mortals besides skills.<br /> <br /> Legacy had Hunters Hunted, so even vanilla mortals had access to an interesting list of options. Numina won't make you as powerful as a full splat, but gives you options they can't easily copy, either.<br /> <br /> Both in the end give you something so if you play a mortal in a Vampire game, you don't feel useless. You may not be as powerful, but you have your own nice toys and everyone has things to do.<br /> <br /> V5 really is limited. For now it's working, but we are really worried that Sullivan may end up with too little space to grow without house rules. <hr />From what I know of the US, there's less overall variation when it comes to cars specifically. A lot of places really go hard on the city simply not being made to be navigated by foot even at short distances.<br /> <br /> It isn't a personal experience, but it's consistent among the experiences I've heard, and I try to have some diversity of sources. Either way the US seems to be quite extreme in this regard by the words of people who lived there and in other countries, it isn't just bad public transportation but an effectively hostile city design for people without a car.<br /> <br /> Again, though, it's what they say. Even if those sources are as diverse as I could find, they may share any number of bias I couldn't notice, so take it with a grain of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T16:10:09-07:00","id":1563715,"title":"","content":"About my character. One thing I wanted with Y\u016bbi was to play a counterpoint to regular Vampire assumptions. That's something I did with ST approval, to be clear upfront.<br /> <br /> What happens when a vampire has a cultural perspective over the condition so different that most assumptions just fall apart? In America we are so immersed in the Christian worldview that the themes of damnation and redemption are obvious.<br /> <br /> But as Japanese they're just exotic to Hoshino Y\u016bbi. For her becoming a vampire is becoming Youkai: inhuman in a strict sense, but also valid as just another place to occupy in the world. It has no inherent spiritual or moral implications. It is what she chooses to make out of it, with no major theological connotations.<br /> <br /> She sees no contradiction in being a predator and a productive member of society, and is feeling the loss of her country more than her pulse. She's delighted with being linked to a dragon because of her Clan, as even knowing they're talking about things like Smaug, her instinct is still to think about the Japanese guardians of weather that symbolize wisdom and compassion. And if suddenly asked about Clan, she's more likely to answer Hoshino than Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Currently she's working on her carving skills in her spare time with a project even a Malkavian could find crazy: she wants to express what she learned about Kindred making netsuke, little statuettes, of the clans, but she wants the pieces to express what she thinks to be the best side of each clan. For that she will carve them as the Shichifukujin, the Seven Luck Gods of Japan. If everything goes well who knows, maybe they even get some help with their current problems from Ebisu, the Kami who cleans the sea.<br /> <br /> The current plan is for each kami to represent two clans, including the Salubri as she was taught about them, so 14 clans for 7 gods. Each piece will be based on a local member of one of the associated clans. The exception will be the Tzimisce, as she's currently planning on basing it not on herself, but her mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T16:46:48-07:00","id":1563720,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That\u2019s very interesting. My character also doesn\u2019t see vampirism as bad as Christian mythology would. Although, she finds her Nosferatu curse pretty hard to deal with even if she got a pretty lenient one as far as VTR Nosferatu curses can go.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve done something similar in my own setting for the Ume house vampire mythological explanation, taking inspiration from actual Shinto myth.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mythological Origin</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The story of Tsukuyomi\u2019s murder of Ukemochi takes a darker turn than the version recorded in the Kojiki.<br /> <br /> Upon her death, Ukemochi cursed Tsukuyomi so that he would never again be able to enjoy any form of food. When evening came, Tsukuyomi found himself starving, slowly dying of hunger. He was then visited by Okage-no-Fukur\u00f4, the Owl of Great Shadow, who suggested that he drink Ukemochi\u2019s blood. Blood, he explained, was not truly food, yet still possessed enough nourishment to sustain him.<br /> Tsukuyomi followed his advice and thanked Okage-no-Fukur\u00f4.<br /> <br /> When Tsukuyomi returned to the heavens, Amaterasu was furious and disgusted by his actions. She refused to ever again set eyes upon her brother and forced him to move to another part of the heavens.<br /> <br /> Once separated from Amaterasu, Tsukuyomi was forced to survive by feeding upon humans, descending to the mortal world after nightfall to drink their blood. He survived this way for some time, but eventually grew lonely and once again sought the counsel of Okage-no-Fukur\u00f4.<br /> <br /> The Owl of Great Shadow taught him a method through which mortals could be helped to achieve ascension. They would first have to be purged of their mortal blood and then infused with the blood of a Kami.<br /> <br /> Thus were the vampires born.<br /> <br /> Vampires are the children of Tsukuyomi and, therefore, his divine descendants. They are known as the Tsuki-no-ko, the Children of the Moon.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Beast and Vampiric Nature</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Although they are half-Kami, all Tsuki-no-ko were once human.<br /> <br /> Their transformation is a violent passage through death, and because of this, every Tsuki-no-ko carries within them a dark energy originating from Yomi, the land of the dead. This energy is infused with Izanami\u2019s fury toward the living and possesses the power to transform a Tsuki-no-ko into anOnry\u014d, a wrathful spirit.<br /> <br /> Every vampire is therefore inhabited by their own inner Onry\u014d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Role of the Tsuki-no-ko</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As beings touched by the Kami, the Tsuki-no-ko possess the potential to attain enlightenment, cast out their inner Onry\u014d, and eventually achieve the status of a true Kami.<br /> <br /> To draw closer to the Kami, a Tsuki-no-ko must learn to control their Onry\u014d and seek the state of veneration offered to them by mortals.<br /> <br /> Within mortal society, the Tsuki-no-ko have a responsibility to inspire veneration while also behaving as Kami themselves. This means granting good fortune to those deserving of it, but also punishing transgressions when necessary.<br /> <br /> The Tsuki-no-ko also have a responsibility to remain part of the living world and to avoid polluting it with the death, pestilence, and misfortune of Yomi that they carry within themselves. They must strive to live in harmony with nature, in the hope that one day they may earn Amaterasu\u2019s forgiveness.<br /> Because of their tainted nature, the Tsuki-no-ko are expected to purify themselves upon awakening each evening and again before returning to their slumber before sunrise.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Kigan</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kigan is the ritualization of the power of the Kami.<br /> <br /> As half-Kami, the Tsuki-no-ko cannot simply command divine forces as they please. Instead, they must petition other Kami and the forces of nature, asking them to lend their power by offering their divine blood as tribute.<br /> <br /> Through Kigan, a Tsuki-no-ko invokes these divine and natural forces and temporarily draws upon their power.<br /> <br /> <br /> </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T16:24:43-07:00","id":1563777,"title":"","content":"The first statuette of her project is already halfway done.<br /> <br /> <b>\u5927\u9ed2\u5929 (Daikokutennyo) \u2014 Ventrue/Hecata</b><br /> <br /> The feminine form of Daikokuten is uncommon but still sometimes seen with the Shichifukujin since the 17th century.<br /> <br /> - Goddess of commerce, the kitchen, and the harvest, she carries Uchide no Kozuchi, the magical mallet that creates the desired goods out of nothing.<br /> <br /> - In feminine form she's a trio with Benzaiten and Kichij\u014dten. Being all three of Hindu origin as the Tridevi, she is the Japanese name of the goddess Parvati/Durga/Kali, consort of Shiva.<br /> <br /> - Patron goddess of cooks.<br /> <br /> - Depiction: dark-skinned, seated on rice bales, with rats signifying plenty, carries the Uchide no Kozuchi and a sack of treasure with gold.<br /> <br /> - She is considered the leader of the Seven or tied with Ebisu.<br /> <br /> - <i>Y\u016bbi's reading: Ventrue</i><br /> - The clan of wealth, authority, table.<br /> - They feed on power and control, and they distribute as they see fit.<br /> - Daikokuten's bag isn't just treasure\u2014it's the means of production.<br /> - They are the mallet that creates Capital\u2014money that makes money.<br /> - Hierarchy and stewardship, first of the bunch appointing leaders.<br /> <br /> - <i>Y\u016bbi's reading: Hecata/Giovanni</i><br /> - Provisioning, harvesting produce and cooking it into sustenance for the household.<br /> - A faceted nature like the layers of family: commerce, crime, magic, it is all there in service to collective wellbeing.<br /> - Generational wealth, your wishes granted by the inheritance of your predecessors, your efforts build the wealth of your successors.<br /> - Leading a family like she leads the Seven.<br /> <br /> - <i>The mold</i><br /> Daikokutennyo standing on two rice bales, mallet raised. One of the bales is branded with a scepter, the other a sword. A crown is in the mallet as a signet mark. The eyes of the goddess are covered by gold coins, and a three headed rat is at the side. <hr /><br /> She's making the netsuke in the image of the Regent Elise Giovanni, since she identifies as Hecata. After the piece is done Y\u016bbi will use it as a master to make a few cast iron molds for ningy\u014dyaki, a doll-like sweet fried cake from Asakusa. Then she'll gift Elise with the original and start distributing or selling the cakes to the local children, using sweet potato cream as a filling for half, dark chocolate with a dash of Asian mint for the other half.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-03T14:44:53-07:00","id":1563808,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oh, that's very cool!<br /> <br /> I remember visiting Benzaiten\u2019s Shrine in Senso-ji, Asakusa. Super crowded with tourists, but still a very beautiful place to visit.<br /> <br /> I remember you mentioned project rules in another thread. How did your group end up handling the project mechanically?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m expecting Benzaiten to be patron of the toreador?<br /> <br /> Do you have ideas for the other clans as well?<br /> </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T02:13:23-07:00","id":1563819,"title":"","content":"Most projects will just be regular Extended rolls, as the ST decided.<br /> <br /> By the way, Y\u016bbi grew up near Sens\u014dji, her main reference on living Shinto is that area and this temple, although Japan has also a number of yearly pilgrimage traditions that encourage the faithful to visit more distant shrines regularly.<br /> <br /> I already have most of the setup done for every clan/god combination, only remains open who will be the vampire model for each netsuke.<br /> <br /> All are going to be made into ningy\u014dyaki molds and standardized fillings, making a proper style of Ningy\u014dyaki for Carcosa is one of her ideas of contribution to the city. <hr /><br /> Since you asked for this one specifically:<br /> <br /> <b>\u5f01\u8ca1\u5929 (Benzaiten) \u2014 Toreador/Tremere</b><br /> <br /> Her depictions as member of the Shichifukujin and regular emphasis in popular depictions to her role as goddess of beauty/art made a lot of important details about Benzaiten become very obscure outside her cult.<br /> <br /> Y\u016bbi knows many of them, her interpretation is also influenced by her historical association with the Hindu Saraswati, the Persian Anahita and her war aspect in Japan up to the 12th century.<br /> <br /> - Goddess of water, music, arts, eloquence, the patron of creative genius and memory.<br /> <br /> - member of the Tridevi as Saraswati, being the consort of Brahma in some depictions and the energy of Creation (shakti). she is also a travel companion to Ugajin, a Shinto snake god or goddess of fertility and harvest.<br /> <br /> - Patron of artists and artisans, those who work with creation.<br /> <br /> - her regular depiction is finely dressed and playing a biwa, her headdress literally includes a tor\u012b gate. The white snake Ugajin rests coiled atop her head, beneath this Tor\u012b, having either the face of an elderly man or a woman of any age.<br /> - but as goddess of victory in war, she has an older depiction without the instrument. In that she has 8 hands and wields an arsenal of bow, arrow, sword, spear, axe, a vajra, an iron wheel and a noose. The vajra is an Indian mace with some serious religious symbolism.<br /> <br /> - Invoked for victory, wealth, skill in crafts and arts, good memory and creative smarts, being with Fukurokuju one of the most sought gods to help with academic tests.<br /> <br /> - While she is a goddess of beauty, she is an academic femininity, less related with family and romance and more with feminine virtues in intellectual and social endeavors. In fact she is said to help with conquest in love, but bringing terrible luck in this area, so much so they say a couple that visit her shrines together won't be together for long after.<br /> <br /> - She's also an accomplished diplomat, with stories about the beasts she &quot;defeated&quot; by explaining how their actions affected others and converting them to Buddhism. She's both guardian and teacher of the Golden Light Sutra, an important book of Buddhist magical prayers and theological teachings.<br /> <br /> - *Y\u016bbi's reading: Toreador*<br /> - The clan of beauty, art, passion. A life that's aesthetic in all its layers.<br /> - Creating or consuming, promote the arts. Benzaiten is all of those, artist, viewer and patron.<br /> - Benzaiten\u2019s biwa is a hidden arsenal for her rarely seen eight arms. Sje achieves victory in every battle, and so the clan isn't about beauty in lieu of other pursuits, but as the means to measure and achieve goals.<br /> - Jealousy and envy accompany the goddess as much as the clan. Her portfolio has love, but all strife that desire can bring comes with it.<br /> - Words are power. As Benten can with words convert dragons, heal the sick and shape the collective memory, so can the diplomats and courtiers of Toreador change lives.<br /> <br /> - *Y\u016bbi's reading: Tremere*<br /> - Art, memory and sweet words are also incantation, the performance of magic.<br /> - If not wise with age, the goddess is still a scholar, a newcomer that brings the mysteries of the Sutras.<br /> - Benten knows many practical arts. She sharpens the mind and teach magical mantras that cure illness, avert disaster or grant protection.<br /> - She also guards sacred magic. It's hers the duty to guard and spread the Golden Light Sutra, and waters with mystical properties, like that of multiplying things.<br /> - Ugajin is a mystery itself guarded with care. May be a forgotten god she's bringing back to light, or may be an inheritor of Fuxi and N\u00fcwa, a figure of occult significance like the secrets of the Warlocks.<br /> <br /> - *The mold*<br /> Benzaiten playing a biwa where a silhouette of an armed octopus is seen. Her yukata has motifs of Japanese symbols used by Onmy\u014d magicians. Ugajin carries a rose in her mouth. <hr /><br /> Her model is a local Tremere that helped her a lot upon arrival. Half the ningy\u014dyaki will have a filling of white bean (Shiroan) to signify the Toreador, but I'm still deciding what I'll use for the Tremere filling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T09:00:15-07:00","id":1563827,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Probably better to run projects as extended rolls, yeah.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Asasuka is truly a beautiful place, the whole area near Sens\u014d-ji is full of shrines. Although it\u2019s technically a buddhist temple, buddhism and Shinto in Japan are pretty interlinked, as I\u2019m sure you\u2019re aware. It\u2019s truly unique and interesting.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I asked about Benzaiten mostly because it\u2019s the only one I knew of, lol.<br /> <br /> If you have others prepared, I\u2019m also interested in reading what you have cooked.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think Toreador being linked to a goddess of war makes sense as well.<br /> <br /> As horrible as it is, war does involve creative thinking and war is often referred to as an art ; Sun Tzu ''Art of war'' translation comes to mind. (Although i haven't read it)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it stands in other languages. In mandarin and japanese, \u2018\u2019 \u5175\u6cd5\u2018\u2019 (b\u012bngf\u01ce/heih\u014d), contained in \u5b6b\u5b50\u5175 (S\u016bnz\u01d0 b\u012bngf\u01ce), is translated as military tactics or if you take both characters individually, it means Soldier and Law respectively.<br /> <br /> In French, we do have \u2018\u2019Art de la guerre\u2019\u2019. So it\u2019s not limited to English only. But English and French are pretty close due to historical influences over one another.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not an expert at all, so take anything i say with a grain of salt, but it seems like there is something like the idea that learning a skill involves more than simply the technical aspect. It also involves the \u2018\u2019way\u2019\u2019 which includes philosophy and spirituality. Art and martial arts appear to be similar in that way. Ky\u016bd\u014d could be something I\u2019d see a toreador get obsessed with. It</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the Yremere filling, maybe red bean? I don\u2019t know if it would taste good mixed with white bean. Or any red filling. I always associated Tremere with the color red. Probably because of Strauss from Bloodline.<br /> </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T17:39:17-07:00","id":1563844,"title":"","content":"Sens\u014dji used to be a syncretic temple, but during the Meiji they moved the Shinto part to other shrines and temples nearby.<br /> <br /> But on top of the folk practices being usually mixed, you can also have the same entity fill a different role depending on religion. So Sens\u014dji is not related to the Shichifukujin, but some of them are part of Buddhism and so they'll be there in this capacity.<br /> <br /> This includes Benzaiten. Her Shinto shrines are usually guarding water sources with alleged mystical powers and focus on the magic water, but in Sens\u014dji she's present as a teacher of Sutras and Buddhist prayers.<br /> <br /> Its main deity is Kannon, though, Bodhisattva of Compassion. The temple guards a statue of Kannon that was found in the nearby river and deemed a miracle. The three fishermen who found the statue are now considered Kami, but they are worshipped in another temple nearby.<br /> <br /> Long story short, the Shichifukujin were at first a thought exercise that got too popular. Really too popular.<br /> <br /> They're not originally related in any way. In the 15th century some scholars were tasked with making an allegory to explain what competent statesmen need, and they decided to bunch 7 gods as exemplars of what they called the 7 virtues of state.<br /> <br /> By design the list sought examples from many places and religions, because they were just meant to be didactic. One is Japanese, other three are from India and three from China, with 2 Buddhist, 2 Hindu and 2 Taoist (with an error, the two are actually variations of a same god).<br /> <br /> All the 7 were gods of good luck in some sense though, and so people really liked the idea of them all working as a fortune granting group, the Shichifukujin became increasingly popular and traditions were built around the group with no direct link to their actual theology. <hr /><br /> The &quot;Art of War&quot; is a common European title for Sun Zi's book, it's the same in every European Language. Also, it's a greatly overestimated book, it isn't bad, but quite basic stuff, it can be summed in a 1 page list without much loss, the rest is poetic phrasing and a couple stories to show how Sun Zi was competent.<br /> <br /> On the meaning of art, I recommend studying the history of the concepts of Techn\u00e9 and Art until the Late Middle Ages, and original Greek foundational works on Aesthetics, understand what it was really about before its stupidity magnification process.<br /> <br /> But basically the modern concept of art that's the fundament of the Fine Arts is actually a semantic aberration built in the 17th century Europe as a tool of cultural dominance. It is an artificial distinction between form and function designed to argue for intellectual inferiority of others without need for actual engagement. <hr /><br /> Red Bean (Anko) is already taken.<br /> <br /> <b>\u6bd8\u6c99\u9580\u5929 (Bishamon) \u2014 Brujah/Banu Haqim</b><br /> <br /> Also known as Bishamonten. This &quot;-ten&quot; in the end means something like &quot;heavenly&quot;, it's a suffix for divine names that denote a kami that live in certain higher planes.<br /> <br /> - Originally the guardian-king Vai\u015brava\u1e47a, tied to Kubera, Hindu god of the north and wealth as much as war.<br /> <br /> - Brother or Husband of Kichij\u014dten.<br /> <br /> - Patron of soldiers and guards.<br /> <br /> - Depiction: standing upright, raised spear, clad in armor and carrying in his left hand the Pagoda of Treasury that holds all wealth of a community, economic or not, he's right foot upon a demonic head.<br /> <br /> - Represent state not as status quo, but institution that guards society and its wealth for the people.<br /> <br /> - Punisher of evil, guardian of the North, the one who enforces. He seeks not dominance, but to care for the faithful.<br /> <br /> - <i>Y\u016bbi's reading: Brujah</i><br /> - The clan of righteous violence and rage directed against abuse.<br /> - They fight oppression, tyranny, corruption of intent. Rebellion is not blind, but to replace the rule of kleptocrats with a proper State.<br /> - Guard and punishes. As the god they say, &quot;No, this ends now.&quot;<br /> - They too protect the pagoda from pilferers, caring for what's socially valuable.<br /> - A foot over the head of tyranny, an illegitimate king falling to the will of the people and the anger of the oppressed.<br /> <br /> - <i>Y\u016bbi's reading: Banu Haqim</i><br /> - Custodians of the kine against the predations of their Kindred, taking the role of judicial protection.<br /> - Violence is only legitimate when sanctioned for a proper purpose. To destroy those who abuse their strength is one such purpose.<br /> - They guard society and a doctrine that keeps it running and safe.<br /> - Warrior's tension between appetite and discipline, to police or indulge.<br /> - If the institutions fail, they're the knife to end the tyrant. If they hold true, they're judges that apply law.<br /> <br /> - <i>The mold</i><br /> Bishamonten in full red armor, spear raised, one foot on an executive. The point of the spear is the symbol of Anarchism, the Pagoda has the name Haqim etched in Standard Arabic.<br /> <br /> Quick explainer, Islam differentiate from most religions in that the main text, the Qur'an, has a strict rule that every faithful has to study it in the original. Translations are allowed to show it to infidels or as linguistic exercises, but actual religious use does not admit anything but the original.<br /> <br /> As a resulting benefit, its language is extremely stable and uniform, serving as a written Lingua Franca for Muslims. They have lots of distinct languages and also lots of variations of Arabic, but any Muslim majority community will teach Standard Arabic that members can use to write stuff that anyone else with similar education can read. Which also means non-Muslims will learn Standard Arabic just because it's useful, and that has been the case for close to 1.400 years.<br /> <br /> I'm between using two models for Bishamon, either a PC or the Sheriff, both Brujah. Brujah Bishamon will have Anko filling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T11:54:40-07:00","id":1563856,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Interesting stuff, I know that Buddhism and Shinto was separated, by institutional force, during the Meiji era. I wasn\u2019t aware that Sens\u014d-ji suffered the same fate.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Between learning Japanese, game preparation, work social duties, etc., I don\u2019t know if I\u2019ll honestly have time to truly inform myself, but I did glance through the Wikipedia page. Thanks for the info.<br /> That being said, I\u2019m not without some background in philosophy. My philosophy bachelor\u2019s degree is a few years away and I haven\u2019t really engaged in philosophy much since, but I remember trying to define what \u2018\u2019Art\u2019\u2019 was never something simple to define.<br /> <br /> The idea to try to define art while denigrating other forms of arts is an old one. I can think of Plato defining art(mimesis) as the \u2018\u2019copy of a copy\u2019\u2019. I remember writing a resume on Aristotle\u2019s response to Plato on mimesis. Aristotle\u2019s response was pretty good.<br /> <br /> As for the 17<sup>th</sup>-century redefinition into fine art to denigrate common folk; that seems typical of the renaissance \u2018\u2019Enlighted\u2019\u2019 philosopher thinking. When you realize that for most renaissance philosopher any time they mention \u2018\u2019Men\u2019\u2019, they don\u2019t mean mankind but actual white men, their ideas lose a lot of their charm. I\u2019ll spare you the infamous incredibly racist quote from Kant.<br /> In general, it seems to be used interchangeably with skill, craft and creative process, however, and I\u2019m fine with that definition. And I\u2019m fine to accept anything as art as long as there\u2019s a genuine belief that one is making art by the creator.<br /> <br /> It gets funkier when we involve AI, but that\u2019s a whole other can of worms. (Outside of the current sociopolitical context, I don\u2019t have strong opinions about AI.)</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Doesn\u2019t all \u5929 (ten) suffix for gods means heavenly? As it\u2019s the character of heaven.<br /> <br /> \u6bd8\u6c99\u9580 would be Bishamon. I\u2019m at the very beginning of my Japanese study, but I know \u2018\u2019\u9580\u2019\u2019 can be read, \u2018\u2019mon.\u2019\u2019 (I had to google the rest to make sure I wasn\u2019t saying complete nonsense.)<br /> <br /> Also cool write up!</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I think I might have encountered an effigy or a depiction of Bishamonten in Toyko.<br /> <br /> Some funny yet slightly embarrassing mistake I made while in a bar held by a very nice Buddhist monk, whom I plan to revisit next year.<br /> <br /> I saw there was a lot of \u2018\u2019demons\u2019\u2019 and I asked if they were evil entities. The monk laughed a bit and told me that no they were Buddhist divinities, they looked scary to scare off evil doers.<br /> Glad I didn\u2019t often him, although the chance was pretty low given that a Monk bartender is atypical to begin with.<br /> <br /> Buddhism is fascinating but I find it so hard to understand as a foreigner. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T19:57:12-07:00","id":1563861,"title":"","content":"Meij\u012b tried to diminish Buddhism's influence because it is a foreign religion and reduced the legitimacy of the nationalist state they were trying to build.<br /> <br /> But overall that's the history of Shinto: it does not, actually, exists. Not as religion, institution, theology, cosmogony, any of such.<br /> <br /> What Japan actually has is a plethora of local traditions and temples that exist independently, whose beliefs, rituals and myths own nothing to each other, just sometimes develop links out of exchanges and syncretism.<br /> <br /> Shinto isn't a common thread linking all those systems, it is a state policy of promotion for all the indigenous beliefs that accept to legitimate their nationalist agenda. They've been doing that since the 6th century, pretending there's a &quot;true nipponic soul&quot; connecting all the temples and practices as long as they promote that the Japanese state has divine lineage and society in the country should organize according to the political prescriptions of the state.<br /> <br /> And Buddhism has never been a part of this as it is an actual organized religion. Even if it has no central authority, it has centralizing tenets and institutions. When locals create their own syncretic traditions about the role of a temple or of figures of the religion, the monks and the temple do not follow suit. They may and do let people have their beliefs, but internally they are still more related to global Buddhism than local folklore. <hr /><br /> I must admit I wasn't paying much attention if the written kanji were following pronunciation/r\u014dmaji spelling, but basically yes. It's not much of a rule just because Japanese don't have a lot of actual rules on how to written kanji, but it is indeed the case that \u5929 should be dropped when calling him Bishamon.<br /> <br /> The important part is to know this &quot;havenly&quot; is in a very specific Japanese sense. Traditionally they distinguish the realm where a deity lives in and/or govern, it doesn't indicate divine status or necessarily a hierarchy, but rather where in the &quot;world tree&quot; so to speak a given deity lives.<br /> <br /> Gods of abstract phenomena, celestial bodies and the like are likely to be identified with \u5929, although using the suffix has other linguistic considerations, while gods of lineages, places, physical phenomena and several others won't. Even something like the myths of a god leading them to move where they live can affect use of the suffix. <hr /><br /> The problem with &quot;demonic&quot; depictions is that it has a lot more cultural assumptions than we are usually told. I personally avoid using the term in many contexts because we are really, really conditioned to think demons are a kind of universal concept when it is nothing of the like even in Europe.<br /> <br /> Buddhism is still at its roots an Indian religion, and there scary deities are common. Take for example that the recurring European/American presentation of Kali as a goddess that revels in wanton bloodlust and destruction is actually an extremely offensive mistake.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, Buddhism is based in the concept that every entity exists within the cycle of reincarnation and their search for Nirvana, so there's no such a thing as innate evil that can be surmised from taxonomy or appearance. Anyone can choose to follow the Path, and even achieve Enlightenment, without ceasing to be who/what they are in this life. <hr /><br /> <b>\u6075\u6bd4\u5bff (Ebisu) \u2014 Lasombra/Ravnos</b><br /> <br /> As everyone and their dog will remind you if you look for the Shichifukujin, Ebisu is set apart in the group by being the only native god in all senses.<br /> <br /> His influence by himself in Japan is staggering, much larger than any of the others. You'll find references and images of Ebisu everywhere, he is used to name places, companies, products, he's legitimately one of the most important and influential gods in Japan despite relative low theological position.<br /> <br /> If you've seen any Japanese brand with a name that reminds his or Evisu, and/or with a mascot that's a laughing man with a fishing rod or fish, those are references to Ebisu, and include from basketball teams to design clothes, beer, cars and whatever else you can imagine.<br /> <br /> - The only of Japanese-origin in the Seven, god of fishing, commerce and hard, honest work. Ebisugao, his smiling face, never wavers. To live is a wonder.<br /> <br /> - ritually paired with Daikokuten in depictions of the Shichifukujin \u2014 the two heads of the ship (I'll talk about the ship later), both patrons of trade. Firstborn of Izanagi and Izanami as Hiruko, the Leech child born without bones or limbs. As the Three Gods of Good Fortune he joins with Daikokuten and Fukurokuju.<br /> <br /> - Patron of fishermen since prehistoric Japan<br /> <br /> - Depicted carrying a fishing rod in one hand and a red sea bream tucked under his left arm, wears a tall <i>Kazaori Eboshi</i> hat. sometimes he's accompanied by jellyfish or fugu and he is said to incarnate as whales, whale-shark, or other marine mega fauna. His depiction has infinite variation as mascot of businesses and their products.<br /> <br /> Obs: because of his relationship to mega fauna fishermen in northern Honsh\u016b are adamantly opposed to whaling. For those people hunting whales not only isn't &quot;Japanese culture and pride&quot;, but is actually active blasphemy.<br /> <br /> - Born disabled because of an error in his parents\u2019 marriage ritual, cast to the sea, he was raised by Ebisu Saburo of the Ainu after reaching the shores of Hokkaid\u014d. He grew bones and strong muscles, but is still hard of hearing and slow to move.<br /> <br /> - He can't hear the call of the kannazuki, the Month Without Gods when all deities of Japan gather at Izumo. Some say because of this he is the only god available to prayer during this period in the rest of the country. Being crippled also means he takes 7 days to finish his most regular task, cleaning the debris in the ocean, bringing it to the shore.<br /> <br /> - <i>Y\u016bbi's reading: Lasombra</i><br /> - Survivalists, they are cast to the dark waters and still live to grow stronger.<br /> - Even their very reflections reject them, but they stay unabated by it.<br /> - The fishing rod becomes a leash into the Deep Dark to pull his fare from the waters of the Abyss, as water is their element. In the dark depths they built their castle,<br /> - If honesty is dubious, their work is still hard, neither taking the easy route or wavering under hardship.<br /> - With their Bane they are the slow crippled of modernity, without the ears, legs and arms of the century.<br /> <br /> - <i>Y\u016bbi's reading: Ravnos</i><br /> - Ebisu has no fixed temple lineage, turning up wherever fishermen are \u2014 by nature without roots.<br /> - Fukunusubi: steal a Daikoku/Ebisu figure for luck at New Year market.<br /> - As the god is left out of kannazuki in Izumo Taisha, is the clan left out of the reunions of the others.<br /> - Living with the wandering tribes of nomads as Ebisu lived with Ainu, a people marginalized in their own land.<br /> - The sea as symbol of dreams and illusions, where Ebisu takes form as animals beyond the reach of a regular disguise or transmutation.<br /> <br /> - <i>The mold</i><br /> Ebisu smiling sitting in a chart, he's with a rod, fish and hat. In the pitch black hat lies a pitch black jellyfish that gives it the look of a dark crown. The chart red wheels are Chakra Wheel with the distinct 16 rays depicted in the flag of the Roma.<br /> <br /> While Y\u016bbi doesn't like executives that much, she is trying to approach the one who's in the coterie with an open mind, so she'll use him as model for Ebisu, making for a curious blend of corporate fashion and a smiling fisherman.<br /> <br /> For the Lasombra filling she'll use \u9ed2\u7df4\u308a\u3054\u307ekuronerigoma, a slightly sweet paste of black sesame seeds, maybe adding some sugar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T08:11:34-07:00","id":1564240,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apologies for the very delayed answer. I have gotten very busy in the last two weeks.<br /> <br /> I technically still am, but I wanted to take the time to at least answer.</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That does align with what I\u2019ve been reading sporadically left and right. I'm not an expert on japanese history, so i usually take a careful approach when making declaration. (Not implying you aren't).</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll be honest, I only caught that because I started studying j\u014dy\u014d kanji a few months ago and now each time I see kanji I try to actually read it.<br /> Kanji are pretty fun to learn honestly.<br /> <br /> Interesting distinction, however, on the japanese definition of heavenly.</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yeah, Demon is a loaded term. I know it has been used to vilify non-christian religions in the past. I didn\u2019t use dit when I asked the monk, but as someone raised in an environment with Christian mythological influences, this was the first word that came to mind when I looked at the depiction. I wouldn\u2019t call them demons either, even though my original reply might have hinted that way.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As for Ebisu, interesting pairing!<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t have thought of mixing Ravnos and Lasombra, but when you think about it\u2026 Illusions &amp; shadows are pretty close thematically.<br /> <br /> I think both readings are also on point.<br /> <br /> Linking Lasombra to abyssal water is also very interesting. I remember reading or hearing that dark water or still in Japanese folklore is often tied to illness or impurity. Thus it makes sense to link the abyss to water.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T11:42:38-07:00","id":1564245,"title":"","content":"The tales of [Lasombra] the Ante and the Clan during his reign also talk a lot about deep 9waters. His castle of shadows is in the water and goes deep, and the Clan explored the lands around and islands within the Mediterranean sea precisely because their main domain was the sea itself, and for along time the Clan was renowned for its seafaring members. <hr /><br /> While their theologies are diverse and their shrines and temples are distinct from each other, the Shichifukujin inspired the rise of a number of traditions around them.<br /> <br /> First is the Takarabune, the Lucky Ship. It's said that the Seven get together for a journey to the heavens in the New Year, so during this time it is customary to depict their ship, Takarabune, and the seven within. As gods of fortune and a popular, informal tradition, the Takarabune is a light hearted depiction where good humor is welcome. They can be funny looking, should be all smiling, and having a Takarabune in your house and even your room during the New Year brings good luck.<br /> <br /> After that comes the Shichifukujin Megumi, a pilgrimage to search them in the following two weeks. The idea is to take those 15 days to visit temples and shrines, or at the very least one statue of each Shichifukujin. Here their not being theologically linked is a feature, as the idea is to visit seven or more different sacred places while looking for them. Completing the pilgrimage with a proper visit to each one is a sure way to increase good luck for the year. <hr /><br /> <b>\u5bff\u8001\u4eba (Jur\u014djin) \u2014 Tzimisce/Salubri</b><br /> <br /> - God of long, wise, good life and of the South Pole Star, where live half of the Immortal Taoists.<br /> <br /> - Shares much of his portfolio and role as Shichifukujin with Fukurokuju, sometimes said to be his grandson, even sometimes to share his body. He was once a human Tao Immortal of the Song Dynasty.<br /> <br /> - Patron to the elderly<br /> <br /> - Depiction: old man with long white beard and a head either bald or with a long and white hair, a small frame less than three shaku high (90cm total), a walking staff from which a scroll dangles. Atop the elongated head sits a kanmuri scholar cap. Usually with deer, crane or tortoise at his side. The other hand may carry a magic fan or a cup of sake.<br /> <br /> - His scroll carries valuable wisdom or special knowledge. For some is the Wisdom of the World, others is the lifespan of every living being, and other yet it is a sutra. Either of those carries the secret for a long and happy life.<br /> <br /> - He has the endurance to reach old age and the patience it requires. If you know to persist and wait, time will help you.<br /> <br /> - <i>Y\u016bbi's reading: Tzimisce</i><br /> - The clan of The Eldest endures in their domains and traditions even beyond transmutation. If Hoshino Y\u016bbi endured 30 years, it was the blessings of Jur\u014djin.<br /> - With their keen perception through Auspex and relationship with land, they carry the wisdom and secrets for a fortunate life.<br /> - Recording spiritual philosophy, the spirits of the land and the secrets of the flesh, scholars of the clan are always expanding their paths to their Tao.<br /> - Scholars who never stop, the clan keeps changing and living, finding the new experiences that keep the growing pace of the Aged Wisdom in the Scroll.<br /> - A clan of land, wisdom, magic and connection to animals, they're with the Deer, Crane and Tortoise.<br /> <br /> - <i>Y\u016bbi's reading: Salubri</i><br /> - Through patience they endured. It was not a longevity taken by force or shrewdness, but calm patience to choose wisely and wait the time to enjoy themselves.<br /> - As healers they grant longevity to others, using their knowledge to bless with what they have.<br /> - Seeing and knowing the souls of people, they have the Wisdom, the Sutra and secret to a long, happy life.<br /> - With their teachings and calling, it is a clan that also lives, even if in hiding, rather than just surviving. A clan that understand that longevity must be with happiness, not mere continued existence.<br /> - Call it what they may, they know to seek the actual Tao enlightenment to cultivate the soul of an Immortal <hr /><br /> Instead of using a vampire, Y\u016bbi plans on using her mother as a model for a female Jur\u014djin. At least her idealized memory of her mother.<br /> <br /> And since she's a Tzimisce herself, the only she knows, the filling for the clan's cakes will just be something she likes: a sweetened cream of Matcha with a touch of vanilla extract and as strong as possible. <hr /><br /> I revised the fillings for each clan. Some changed completely:<br /> <br /> Ventrue - kuri kinton, a mix of candied chestnut and yellow sweet potato. It's usually served as a dish in some occasions and colorized for maximum golden shine to attract wealth.<br /> <br /> Hecata - honeyed umeboshi. It is a fermented pickle made with a Japanese apricot called Ume, usually called Japanese Plum (but it's not actually a plum). It's traditional, healthy, a weird but pleasant taste. Usually it's salty, but it isn't uncommon to wash the salt, add honey and mix in sweets.<br /> <br /> Toreador - Kabocha paste with spice. This is a pumpkin variety of Japanese origin that's way sweeter than any other gourd, but it's also one of the few traditional Japanese ingredients the US produce is deemed of as high quality as the Japanese for confectionery. Add black pepper and some browned butter, preferably butter from Hokkaid\u014d.<br /> <br /> Tremere - Beni Imo. It's a very sweet potato from Okinawa that's violently purple. You can't get much more magical, just add some sugar, as it isn't still the sweetest potato in Japan.<br /> <br /> Brujah - Sakura paste with shis\u014d. The paste can be made with the pickled flower or just extract, and usually has a pastel pink color, but shis\u014d is an Asian mint that can be violently red, turning the Sakura cream into blood while the mint packs a punch of flavor.<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim - The inspiration for this is Haft Mewa, a Persian sweet made with seven nuts or fruits (actually most people nowadays use any number) and a sweet liquid like rose water or syrup. Here it will be a paste of dates with mashed pistachios, and a syrup mixed with cardamom.<br /> <br /> Lasombra - Black sesame paste, sweetened with mirin, an extremely sweet rice wine used for cooking. Real Teriyaki sauce is made with it, for example.<br /> <br /> Ravnos - Doce-de-Leite, a caramelized milk candy, made with kokuto and yukishio, sugar and salt with high mineral content and peculiar taste from Okinawa. Y\u016bbi thinks the archetype for Japanese Ravnos would be from Okinawa, a people similarly dominated by imperialist big empires and later treated as second class and thieves around the lands who exploited them.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce - As said, Matcha with vanilla. Y\u016bbi likes it, her mother liked it, that's all that matter.<br /> <br /> Salubri - Yuzu gelly. It's a Japanese citrus variety, sweet but very healthy and good for summer. To add some spice, ginger, hard to be more universal than that. Sesame and ginger are the most widespread ingredients used here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}